Pre-trained weights for the EAC-mp (EAC-Net) model.

EAC-Net is a charge density prediction model based on Equivariant Atomic Contributions (EAC), which decomposes the electronic density at spatial grid points into equivariant contributions from neighboring atoms. This formulation enables the model to simultaneously capture directional dependencies as well as translational and rotational symmetries (see the [EAC-Net paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.04052) and [repository](https://github.com/qin2xue3jian4/EAC-Net) for details).

The model is trained on CHGCAR-derived data obtained and processed from the Materials Project: the training set contains 48,183 frames, with 5,000 grid points randomly sampled per frame (see [dataset entry](https://zenodo.org/records/16990467) for details). When using this model, please cite both the EAC-Net paper (arXiv:2508.04052) and the appropriate references for the Materials Project.
